# A quantum cellular automaton (a reversible partitioned CA), modeled by the kernel. A QCA evolves a line of cells by a
# LOCAL rule that must be reversible (unitary), so the whole evolution is invertible and information is conserved, exactly
# the property the knit collision has on the mesh. The model is a four-cell ring partitioned into two blocks; each beat
# applies a controlled-NOT inside each block (the second cell is flipped by the first). The kernel proves that the GLOBAL
# step, the whole-ring update, is its own inverse: applying it twice returns every one of the sixteen configurations to
# itself, so the dynamics run backward as well as forward. Global reversibility emerges from local reversibility, the
# discrete root of unitarity and of the substrate's reversible bulk.

form bit
  case off
  case on

# Exclusive or, the reversible primitive (its own inverse).
task xor
  take a, like bit
  take b, like bit
  like bit
  fork case, read a
    case off
      send back
        read b
    case on
      fork case, read b
        case off
          send back
            make on
        case on
          send back
            make off

# A configuration of the four-cell ring.
form grid
  case cells
    link c0, like bit
    link c1, like bit
    link c2, like bit
    link c3, like bit

# The global step: one beat. Inside block one (cells 0,1) the first cell flips the second; inside block two (cells 2,3)
# likewise. A controlled-NOT in each block, the local reversible rule applied across the whole ring at once.
task step
  take g, like grid
  like grid
  fork case, read g
    case cells
      link c0
      link c1
      link c2
      link c3
      send back
        make cells
          bind c0
            read c0
          bind c1
            call xor
              read c1
              read c0
          bind c2
            read c2
          bind c3
            call xor
              read c3
              read c2

# THE GLOBAL STEP IS REVERSIBLE: step (step g) = g, for every one of the sixteen configurations. The whole-ring update is
# its own inverse, because each block's controlled-NOT is, so the QCA can be run backward. Proved by simultaneous case
# analysis on all four cells.
rule global-step-is-reversible
  seat a, like bit
  seat b, like bit
  seat c, like bit
  seat d, like bit
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call step
        call step
          make cells
            bind c0
              read a
            bind c1
              read b
            bind c2
              read c
            bind c3
              read d
      make cells
        bind c0
          read a
        bind c1
          read b
        bind c2
          read c
        bind c3
          read d
  fold a, b, c, d
